======================================================================
2. EXECUTION-EVIDENCE CLASSIFICATION
======================================================================

STATUS A — PLANNED

The simulation is part of the predefined experimental design but no
execution artifact has yet been identified.

STATUS B — DOCUMENTED / REPORTED

The simulation or its numerical output is represented in a recovered
figure, table, workbook, note, or narrative source, but the underlying
machine-readable or native computational execution artifact has not yet
been recovered.

STATUS C — EXECUTED — EVIDENCE RECOVERED

An execution artifact has been identified, such as:

- COMSOL .mph model containing the relevant solution
- COMSOL result export
- numerical result export
- solver log
- batch execution record
- patient-specific simulation output
- reproducible computational execution record

STATUS D — VERIFIED

Execution evidence exists and the corresponding result has passed the
applicable predefined verification checks.

STATUS E — MANUSCRIPT-REPORTED

The result has sufficient provenance from patient input through
computational execution and verification to support inclusion as a
quantitative manuscript result.

IMPORTANT:

STATUS B must not automatically be upgraded to STATUS C.

STATUS C must not automatically be upgraded to STATUS D.

STATUS D must not automatically be upgraded to STATUS E.

