13. PROHIBITED RECOVERY PRACTICES
======================================================================

The following practices are prohibited:

1. Back-calculating patient-level values from group means.

2. Inventing missing COMSOL outputs.

3. Changing reported values solely to make figures and tables agree.

4. Treating graphical appearance as proof of solver execution.

5. Treating a planned simulation as an executed simulation.

6. Treating a documented value as a verified value without evidence.

7. Creating artificial COMSOL logs after the fact and representing them as
   historical execution logs.

8. Reconstructing an undocumented parameter solely to reproduce a desired
   numerical result.

9. Calling astronaut or external physiological comparisons "independent
   validation" without establishing the calibration/validation split.

